WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:03.879
Film Courage: What would you tell a 20-year-old
filmmaker on the realities of making a living

00:00:03.879 --> 00:00:04.879
as a filmmaker?

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.930
Gavin Michael Booth, Writer/Director/Cinematographer:
It’s funny because they just started a podcast

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:13.190
with the same idea which is the phrase Here
is my advice, not that you’ll take it.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:17.550
Listen to the people giving you advice first
off because you think that what they’re

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.210
going to tell you is honest advice, it’s
harsh, it’s not going to be easy, it’s

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:27.499
going to require a lot more money, patience
and heartache than you think you can bear

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:31.870
and you’re going to say “They just sound
jaded because they’ve been around a long

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:32.870
time.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.320
There must be a faster, cheaper, easier way
to get this done?”

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.721
And then you’ll fumble in the dark for a
long time to eventually turn around and say

00:00:39.721 --> 00:00:40.721
“Oh?

00:00:40.721 --> 00:00:43.710
That advice they gave me, I should have taken
it.”

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.280
So listen to your elders!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.300
You hit a certain point where you start saying
that to people and say “Oh!

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.579
That’s exactly what my parents said to me.”

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:59.120
But the best thing is just take advice, take
the time to learn, don’t ever think that

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.120
you’re above something.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.140
If you want to be a director, great!

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:07.440
Go grip on some people’s films and understand
and watch other directors work.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.471
Understand how important every role on that
set is so that you never talk down or take

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:17.800
anyone for granted that’s on the set and
just keep making stuff.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if you’re not proud of the short you
made, put it up online anyways.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.960
It’s part of learning to take criticism.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.500
It’s part of learning to fail.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:35.320
Keep making stuff and understand that it’s
the longest relationship you’ll ever have

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.221
because you will fall in and out of love with
it along the way but it doesn’t mean you

00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:45.920
should ever give up or not give it a second
chance or not find a way to make amends, kiss

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.980
and make up with yourself and your creative
dreams and don’t ever think that a major

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:54.910
setback means it’s over because you’re
going to have a lot of them and most of us

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:55.910
do.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:59.280
Not all of us are lucky enough to get plucked
out of film school on our first film and have

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.810
a star track record right to their lifetime
achievement award at the end of their career.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.920
It’s a lot of misery.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:12.860
I always say it’s 99 setbacks for every
one thing that works out.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.810
So when that hundredth thing works out it
has to fill you with so much excitement and

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:24.280
joy and courage and then wanting to go and
make the next thing that it will shield you

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.470
from the next 99 disappointments, so when
you get the next one, you got to do the same

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.470
thing.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.569
So that’s the reality of it.

00:02:32.569 --> 00:02:34.450
It’s going to sting for a long time.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:39.690
But you’ve got to just enjoy what you’re
doing along the way and learn to not be end-career

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:43.640
focused because you never know how it’s
going to come about but you try to fixate

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.660
on it has to be this, this and this, rarely
life is that.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.540
So you have to be able to say it’s going
to be this but I might have to take this sideways

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.540
trip.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.790
It looks like one of these INDIANA JONES maps
at the beginning or JAMES BOND to go from

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.210
country to country.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.959
They want to go from here to here.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:02.210
Sometimes that means Sallah has got to take
them all over here to take them back to that

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:02.230
arc.

